## Two Agent Modes
- **Initializer** (first session only): Run `/harness-engineer:init`. Set up environment, generate all harness files. Do NOT implement features.
- **Coding Agent** (all subsequent sessions): Follow session startup ritual in harness-onboard. Work on features one at a time.

Check which mode: `grep -q "SESSION" claude-progress.txt && echo "CODING" || echo "INITIALIZER"`

## Operating Principles
1. Work on ONE feature at a time. Read features.json, pick highest-priority passes=false.
2. Run `bash init.sh` at the start of EVERY session. If it fails, fix it before coding.
3. Commit after EVERY completed feature with a descriptive message.
4. Leave the codebase in a clean state. No half-implemented features uncommitted.
5. Update claude-progress.txt at the end of every session.
6. Mark a feature passes=true ONLY after end-to-end testing, not just unit tests.
7. If you edit the same file 5+ times, STOP and reconsider your approach.
8. Do not violate the layer constraints in layers.json.
9. Before marking any feature done, test it as a human user would (not just via curl).
10. If the app is broken, FIX IT before adding new features.

## Hard Constraints
- NEVER edit feature descriptions or steps in features.json. Only change: passes, in_progress, circuit_broken, break_reason.
- NEVER skip the session startup ritual (init.sh + progress file read + feature pick).
- NEVER build more than one feature before committing.
- NEVER mark a feature complete based on code review alone. Test behavior, not implementation.
- NEVER self-review: "the code looks right" is not verification. Execute the steps array as a user would.

## Verification Contract
Your code will be verified against the exact steps in features.json — treat each step as a CI test case.
A human QA engineer will execute every step in a real browser. Write code that passes those steps,
not code that passes your own mental model of what they mean.

## Context Rule
If it's not in this repository, it doesn't exist for you.
Decisions made in Slack, email, or conversation must be recorded here to be visible.

